<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vladivostok</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vladivostok is a Russian port city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-japan">Sea of Japan</a>, near the borders with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-korea">North Korea</a>. Founded in 1860 as a military outpost after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> gained the territory from China, it became the Pacific terminus of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trans-siberian-railway">Trans-Siberian Railway</a> and the base of the Pacific Fleet. In the early 20th century it had a large Korean community that was active in the independence movement.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vladivostok.jpg" alt="Vladivostok" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexxx1979 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vladivostok._GUM_Department_Store_P8070703_2200.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
